686
00:30:21.750 --> 00:30:23.550
Let well enough alone.

687
00:30:23.830 --> 00:30:24.430
Oh, no.

688
00:30:24.890 --> 00:30:27.970
His campaign slogan was let well enough alone?

689
00:30:28.090 --> 00:30:28.350
Yep.

690
00:30:28.350 --> 00:30:29.550
What does that even mean?

691
00:30:29.550 --> 00:30:30.110
I don't know.

692
00:30:30.230 --> 00:30:32.070
This is why it's the old timer category.

693
00:30:33.110 --> 00:30:35.410
Now, from the category, keep it simple.

694
00:30:35.790 --> 00:30:35.970
Okay.

695
00:30:36.710 --> 00:30:37.210
Dwight D.

696
00:30:37.370 --> 00:30:41.210
Eisenhower, also known as Ike, election 1952.

697
00:30:41.330 --> 00:30:42.090
I know this one.

698
00:30:42.290 --> 00:30:43.370
I like Ike.

699
00:30:43.710 --> 00:30:44.190
Exactly.

700
00:30:44.590 --> 00:30:45.290
Keep it simple.

701
00:30:46.010 --> 00:30:47.910
Next one, and keep it simple.

702
00:30:48.470 --> 00:30:49.190
Dwight D.

703
00:30:49.490 --> 00:30:51.350
Eisenhower again in 1956.

704
00:30:52.590 --> 00:30:54.010
I still like Ike.

705
00:30:54.430 --> 00:30:56.490
Oh, there you go.

706
00:30:57.330 --> 00:31:02.730
And now from the puntastic category, Ulysses S.

707
00:31:02.890 --> 00:31:04.990
Grant, 1872.

708
00:31:05.990 --> 00:31:07.970
Grant us another term.

709
00:31:08.590 --> 00:31:09.230
Wow.

710
00:31:09.470 --> 00:31:09.770
Mm-hmm.

711
00:31:09.890 --> 00:31:10.430
Mm-hmm.

712
00:31:10.530 --> 00:31:16.150
I was very torn within myself whether to label this category puntastic or wah-wah.

713
00:31:16.630 --> 00:31:17.230
I see.

714
00:31:17.490 --> 00:31:17.850
Okay.

715
00:31:19.050 --> 00:31:19.870
Alfred M.

716
00:31:20.030 --> 00:31:21.890
Landon, election 1936.

717
00:31:22.390 --> 00:31:24.970
Let's make it a Landon slide.

718
00:31:26.410 --> 00:31:27.450
Wah-wah.

719
00:31:28.630 --> 00:31:29.850
And Thomas E.

720
00:31:29.950 --> 00:31:31.550
Dewey, election of 1944.

721
00:31:32.350 --> 00:31:34.030
Do we or don't we?

722
00:31:34.530 --> 00:31:35.050
No.

723
00:31:35.550 --> 00:31:36.870
No, that's not real.

724
00:31:37.010 --> 00:31:37.750
It is real.

725
00:31:37.910 --> 00:31:38.930
Do we or don't we?

726
00:31:39.090 --> 00:31:40.190
Do we or don't we?

727
00:31:40.410 --> 00:31:43.130
Why are you even giving people the option to don't we?

728
00:31:43.250 --> 00:31:43.770
I know.

729
00:31:43.930 --> 00:31:45.150
In your campaign slogan.

730
00:31:45.410 --> 00:31:45.590
Well.

731
00:31:46.050 --> 00:31:47.590
Lastly, from the hey now.

732
00:31:47.850 --> 00:31:48.530
Category.

733
00:31:49.070 --> 00:31:52.290
Al Smith, election 1928.

734
00:31:52.630 --> 00:31:53.230
Al Smith?

735
00:31:53.450 --> 00:31:55.290
Someone named Al Smith ran for president?

736
00:31:55.430 --> 00:31:56.050
Yes, Jenna.

737
00:31:56.190 --> 00:32:01.410
In 1928, campaign slogan, make your wet dreams come true.

738
00:32:01.490 --> 00:32:01.540
No.

739
