01:06:33.100 --> 01:06:33.420
Okay.

1513
01:06:33.920 --> 01:06:38.000
Near my house is one of those, like, fruit basket companies.

1514
01:06:38.300 --> 01:06:38.560
Okay.

1515
01:06:38.560 --> 01:06:43.240
You know where you can get, like, the strawberries that look like little tuxedos, but they're

1516
01:06:43.240 --> 01:06:43.800
in a basket.

1517
01:06:43.800 --> 01:06:46.640
Or it's like pineapple on a stick, but half of it has chocolate.

1518
01:06:46.800 --> 01:06:47.360
You know what I'm saying?

1519
01:06:47.360 --> 01:06:47.720
I do.

1520
01:06:47.940 --> 01:06:48.140
Okay.

1521
01:06:48.640 --> 01:06:49.860
I'm going to get one of those.

1522
01:06:50.000 --> 01:06:50.200
Okay.

1523
01:06:50.520 --> 01:06:52.680
And I'm going to go to your windowless building.

1524
01:06:52.740 --> 01:06:53.100
Yes.

1525
01:06:53.220 --> 01:06:54.900
And I'm going to say, I have a delivery for you.

1526
01:06:55.040 --> 01:06:55.860
It's a fruit basket.

1527
01:06:56.380 --> 01:06:56.680
Yeah.

1528
01:06:56.860 --> 01:06:57.500
That's my plan.

1529
01:06:57.760 --> 01:07:02.480
And then what if, like, you can't tell what it is from the lobby?

1530
01:07:02.660 --> 01:07:06.880
Are you just going to be, like, a chatty delivery person that's like, oh, what do you guys do

1531
01:07:06.880 --> 01:07:07.240
here?

1532
01:07:07.740 --> 01:07:08.060
Yeah.

1533
01:07:08.240 --> 01:07:09.060
What's your business?

1534
01:07:09.440 --> 01:07:09.620
Yeah.

1535
01:07:09.620 --> 01:07:15.360
Or I could come and be a disgruntled neighbor and say, hey, we've had some noise complaints.

1536
01:07:15.760 --> 01:07:17.040
I like the fruit idea.

1537
01:07:17.260 --> 01:07:18.400
I feel like it's more me.

1538
01:07:18.640 --> 01:07:19.760
Well, it's more you.

1539
01:07:19.860 --> 01:07:21.260
It's going to be easier role for you to play.

1540
01:07:21.420 --> 01:07:25.620
And then also, I just think the hospitality of it is going to open them up.

1541
01:07:25.800 --> 01:07:26.480
You know what I mean?

1542
01:07:26.580 --> 01:07:27.300
It's going to be.

1543
01:07:27.560 --> 01:07:27.900
Yeah.

1544
01:07:28.100 --> 01:07:28.200
Yeah.

1545
01:07:28.400 --> 01:07:30.980
Who's the fruit from, if they ask?

1546
01:07:32.200 --> 01:07:32.980
The city.

1547
01:07:33.620 --> 01:07:35.420
Thank you for doing business here.

1548
01:07:40.230 --> 01:07:42.690
Maybe a good time for me to tell you I'm really bad at lying.

1549
01:07:43.910 --> 01:07:44.670
I know.

1550
01:07:45.870 --> 01:07:48.670
But I think you're very good at acting.

1551
01:07:49.110 --> 01:07:49.710
I am good at acting.

1552
01:07:49.710 --> 01:07:50.410
So this is a role.

1553
01:07:50.410 --> 01:07:51.470
This is not a lie.

1554
01:07:51.630 --> 01:07:51.730
Right.

1555
01:07:51.730 --> 01:07:54.990
This is a character that we're bringing onto the street.

1556
01:07:55.290 --> 01:07:55.430
Yes.

1557
01:07:55.690 --> 01:07:57.010
Think of it as performance art.

1558
01:07:57.150 --> 01:07:58.050
It's performance art.

1559
01:07:58.210 --> 01:08:00.170
I did a lot of that back in my improv days.

1560
01:08:00.450 --> 01:08:03.830
We'll get back to you, everyone, on the windowless building by my house.

1561
01:08:04.430 --> 01:08:05.170
I'm excited.

1562
01:08:05.890 --> 01:08:09.470
Well, we're about to have some interviews with people from the UK.

1563
01:08:09.790 --> 01:08:11.230
First up is David Brent.

1564
01:08:11.470 --> 01:08:12.330
It's over video.

1565
01:08:12.690 --> 01:08:16.210
He basically says if they're looking for a leader, he's ready.

1566
01:08:16.410 --> 01:08:17.210
When does he start?

1567
01:08:17.450 --> 01:08:22.430
So Paul Lieberstein reached out to Ricky Gervais about doing an in-person cameo as one of the

1568
01:08:22.430 --> 01:08:22.930
applicants.

1569
01:08:23.130 --> 01:08:27.090
And Ricky really wanted to do it, but he was like working on another project at the time

1570
01:08:27.090 --> 01:08:28.250
and he couldn't travel to LA.

1571
01:08:28.590 --> 01:08:33.590
So first he pitched the idea of filming something in the UK.

1572
01:08:33.690 --> 01:08:35.090
Like this was very elaborate.

1573
01:08:35.890 --> 01:08:36.970
It was so nice of him, though.

1574
01:08:37.170 --> 01:08:43.670
He was like, I'll build like your lobby area and then I'll film my side of it.

1575
01:08:43.770 --> 01:08:46.430
And maybe he's the last applicant.

1576
01:08:46.810 --> 01:08:49.810
And Pam's kind of like shutting down the office for the day.

1577
01:08:49.850 --> 01:08:55.470
And he walks in and then it would cut to me in the United States just sort of saying

1578
01:08:55.470 --> 01:08:57.190
like, sorry, the interviews are over.

1579
01:08:57.190 --> 01:08:59.990
And then he could also then have like a talking head.

1580
01:09:01.270 --> 01:09:07.790
Or he said, I could just film like a video interview and you could use that.

1581
01:09:08.490 --> 01:09:11.190
And Paul was like, I think that'll work better.

1582
01:09:11.370 --> 01:09:15.570
I think, you know, that was to build the lobby and then get all the lighting right and everything.

1583
01:09:15.670 --> 01:09:17.090
What if it didn't cut together right?

1584
01:09:17.110 --> 01:09:17.510
Right, right.

1585
01:09:17.510 --> 01:09:18.930
That could be like a little tricky.

1586
01:09:19.430 --> 01:09:22.910
So Ricky sent in four options of interviews.

1587
01:09:23.370 --> 01:09:24.630
We picked this one.

1588
01:09:24.850 --> 01:09:29.190
I bet he did that so fast because that character is just so easy for him.

1589
01:09:29.410 --> 01:09:29.630
Yeah.

1590
01:09:29.930 --> 01:09:33.490
I mean, I could watch him do 70 interviews as that character.

1591
01:09:34.130 --> 01:09:38.390
The next person from the UK to interview is going to be Nellie Bertram.

1592
01:09:38.390 --> 01:09:39.250
Yes.

1593
01:09:40.150 --> 01:09:42.590
Catherine Tate plays Nellie Bertram.

1594
01:09:43.090 --> 01:09:45.450
My gosh, she is amazing.

1595
01:09:45.910 --> 01:09:47.250
Such a funny comedian.

1596
01:09:47.650 --> 01:09:50.650
Had her own show in the UK, which is so funny.

1597
01:09:51.070 --> 01:09:52.110
She's hilarious.

1598
01:09:52.430 --> 01:09:55.270
She's another person I could just watch, read the phone book.

1599
01:09:55.470 --> 01:09:58.530
I love that I keep referencing a phone book that no one has anymore.

1600
01:09:59.650 --> 01:10:01.550
But Catherine is so talented.

1601
01:10:01.770 --> 01:10:05.770
You know, in the shooting draft, they had a different version of the scene that as I read it,

1602
01:10:05.850 --> 01:10:06.770
I could hear her voice.

1603
01:10:06.890 --> 01:10:07.630
It was so funny.

1604
01:10:07.630 --> 01:10:10.310
And then this scene is hilarious to me.

1605
01:10:10.570 --> 01:10:12.450
She just keeps waffling.

1606
01:10:12.610 --> 01:10:15.230
She's like, first, she's like, no cubicles.

1607
01:10:15.410 --> 01:10:16.470
And then they're like, hmm.

1608
01:10:16.590 --> 01:10:18.090
And she's like, definitely cubicles.

1609
01:10:18.250 --> 01:10:20.050
And then she's like, no, no, no, no cubicles.

1610
01:10:20.190 --> 01:10:21.250
Everyone just sits on the floor.

1611
01:10:22.110 --> 01:10:23.490
Everybody is their own boss.

1612
01:10:23.630 --> 01:10:25.390
No, everybody's somebody's boss.

1613
01:10:25.470 --> 01:10:26.990
And she's just going back and forth.

1614
01:10:27.550 --> 01:10:32.210
So I guess Catherine Tate said yes immediately, like everyone else.

1615
01:10:32.330 --> 01:10:35.970
But she was in rehearsals for a play when this was shooting.

1616
01:10:36.490 --> 01:10:38.910
And she came to do our episode.

1617
01:10:39.130 --> 01:10:42.630
She was in the United States for like 36 hours.

1618
01:10:42.890 --> 01:10:43.390
Oh, my God.

1619
01:10:43.530 --> 01:10:45.990
She flew in, kind of came directly to set.

1620
01:10:46.150 --> 01:10:50.250
And then I think she left the very next day because she had to get back for rehearsals.

1621
01:10:50.250 --> 01:10:51.510
Is that crazy?

1622
01:10:51.790 --> 01:10:53.110
That is just boss lady.

1623
01:10:53.790 --> 01:10:57.930
I wanted to read you guys one little thing that was in the shooting draft about the very

1624
01:10:57.930 --> 01:10:58.830
end of her interview.

1625
01:10:59.270 --> 01:11:01.190
It didn't air, but I thought it was very funny.

1626
01:11:01.610 --> 01:11:04.090
She says to Toby, well, what are you offering?

1627
01:11:04.270 --> 01:11:08.270
And Toby says, well, and before he can finish, she says, right, I'll take it.

1628
01:11:08.310 --> 01:11:08.790
Need a job.

1629
01:11:08.870 --> 01:11:09.190
Desperate.

1630
01:11:09.290 --> 01:11:09.670
Good match.

1631
01:11:09.770 --> 01:11:10.210
Sloppy match.

1632
01:11:10.350 --> 01:11:10.510
Whatever.

1633
01:11:11.130 --> 01:11:12.010
Good match.

1634
01:11:12.170 --> 01:11:12.930
Sloppy match.

1635
01:11:13.130 --> 01:11:13.390
Whatever.

1636
01:11:15.150 --> 01:11:16.170
That's pretty great.

1637
01:11:16.830 --> 01:11:17.110
All right.

1638
